From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Silicon Bakery (t6020 port)" <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:42:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] VUI colour description from the V4L2 colorimetry

Write the SPS VUI signal-type group (video_signal_type, video_format 5,
full range, colour_description) for H.264 and HEVC from the OUTPUT
format's colorspace / xfer_func / ycbcr_enc / quantization, mapped to
H.273 code points. Only when the application set any of the four at
S_FMT (enc_vui=1, the default; enc_vui=0 never): an untouched format
keeps vui_parameters_present_flag 0, the stream every release has sent.

Wire fields:
- H.264 [FW] SPS::vui_parameters (13.5 H14S 0x18c68), SPS block at wire
  0x105B0: present 0x109F4 (+0x444), video_signal_type 0x109F7, format
  0x109F8, full_range 0x109FC, colour_description 0x10A00, primaries /
  transfer / matrix 0x10A04 / 0x10A08 / 0x10A0C. The writer has no
  aspect_ratio_idc, overscan_appropriate, timing or HRD syntax behind
  their flags, so every other VUI flag stays 0. These are the bytes
  macOS 13.5 user space fills with 1/5/1/2/2/2 [KEXT13.5 docs/85].
- HEVC [FW] HEVC_SPS::vui_parameters (0x1d140), SPS-relative: present
  +0x1C30, video_signal_type +0x1C41, format +0x1C44, full_range +0x1C48,
  colour_description +0x1C4C, primaries/transfer/matrix +0x1C50/54/58.
[LIVE] macOS 27.2 writes VUI 9/16/9 for an HDR10 session; no HDR SEI.
Untested on hardware.
---
